6. THE MECHANICAL SPREAD POINT
======================================================================================================================
  F is DEFINED by the 50d crossing below the 200d. So the 50d-200d spread at E entry, and the rate at which it is
  closing, are near-tautological predictors of BREAK: a narrow, shrinking spread simply needs fewer down sessions to cross.
  BREAK    n=16  spread% at entry: mean  2.65 median  2.79 min  0.07 max  7.06 | 20-session spread change: mean -0.62 median -1.08 | flat-price sessions to cross: median   26 (min 3, max 137) | episode length median   16
  REVERSAL n=16  spread% at entry: mean  4.07 median  3.04 min  0.02 max 11.08 | 20-session spread change: mean -0.06 median -0.24 | flat-price sessions to cross: median   25 (min 8, max 102) | episode length median    6
  Per BREAK episode: spread at entry, sessions to cross if price flatlined at the entry close, actual E length, and the
