  MECHANICAL POINT: an E entry needs QQQ below 0.99 x SMA200, so on the last D day price is at most a session's move above the 200d;
  gap200 < 2 % on that day is all but guaranteed (the 2020-03 entries are the exception by gap and are caught by breadth). The gate
  therefore holds the D row as cash on the last D day of EVERY D -> E transition, and the carry-over rule carries cash: it is live.
  -> under the CURRENT design the carry-over rule acts on 0 proxy and 0 real episodes: it is a no-op for every k and equals live.
     No k sweep, permutation or bootstrap is run for it. The only path by which a carry-over could matter is if the D gate were ever removed.

